  "label": "Nazi Concentration Camp",
  "description": "A facility established by Nazi Germany during World War II for the imprisonment, forced labor, and mass murder of millions of people, including Jews, Roma, Poles, Soviet prisoners of war, and others. Buchenwald was one of the largest and most notorious camps. The image depicts a crematorium within such a camp, which was used for the systematic extermination of prisoners.",
